("libraries often recommend invalidating only when the last pending mutation settles ⚠ verify (e.g. checking the number of in-flight mutations for that key before invalidating).","TanStack Query's docs recommend invalidating only when the last pending mutation settles: `if (queryClient.isMutating({ mutationKey }) === 1) invalidate`. Verified: inside `onSettled` the settling mutation still counts (A settled with `isMutating` = 2, B settled with 1), so the check is `=== 1`, not `=== 0`."),
